### HAUL – least-privilege setup (run once, as an admin, e.g. in Graph Explorer)
### 1) App registration "HAUL - <client>":
###    API permissions -> Microsoft Graph -> Application -> Lists.SelectedOperations.Selected -> Grant admin consent
###    (Sites.Selected also works, but then the app can write to the whole site, not just one library.)
###    Certificates & secrets -> Certificates -> upload haul-<client>.cer. No client secret.

### 2) Find the site and library IDs
GET https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0/sites/fabrikamit.sharepoint.com:/sites/ClientDropZone
GET https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0/sites/{site-id}/lists?$select=id,displayName
GET https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0/sites/{site-id}/lists/{list-id}/drive?$select=id   
### -> this id is the DriveId in haul.config.json

### 3) Grant the app "write" on that ONE library (needs Sites.FullControl.All, or Sites.Selected + FullControl on the site)
POST https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0/sites/{site-id}/lists/{list-id}/permissions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "grantedToV2": { "application": { "id": "{haul-app-client-id}", "displayName": "HAUL - Contoso Dental" } },
  "roles": ["write"]
}

### 4) Create the top folder once (HAUL creates one sub-folder per computer name)
POST https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0/drives/{drive-id}/root/children
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "PM", "folder": {}, "@microsoft.graph.conflictBehavior": "fail" }

### Revoke later: GET .../lists/{list-id}/permissions, then DELETE .../lists/{list-id}/permissions/{permission-id}
